{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartel Charter War","logline":"When the Bridge Wardens challenge the Drift Cartel's charter, cartographer Veya and toll-master Kael, once apprentices together, race to control the last stable skybridge routes while every isle is forced to choose a side.","theme":"Control costs more than it gains; shared truth outlasts hoarded power.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Charter Cracks","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"The Fading Bridges","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya uses her wind-sight to finish a chart showing which skybridges will fail first. The chart suggests the Cartel's charter routes are among the most unstable.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to complete a chart of a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and prove her mentor's theory.","conflict":"Her wind-sight readings contradict the Cartel's published route guarantees, and she stubbornly refuses to second-guess her own data.","outcome":"Veya finishes a chart showing the charter routes are failing, and decides to carry it to the Wardens rather than publish it at the Academy."},{"id":"scn_emberroost_accusation","title":"Cables of Suspicion","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya presents her chart to the Bridge Wardens. They reveal that cloudstone supplies for cable braiding have been quietly diverted, and they blame Kael and the Cartel. The Wardens resolve to formally challenge the Cartel Charter.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to act on her chart and reinforce the failing bridges.","conflict":"The Wardens' leaders want to use her chart as a political weapon against the charter rather than as a safety tool, and Veya fears becoming an ambitious instrument.","outcome":"The Wardens file a formal challenge to the Cartel Charter and Veya agrees to let them cite her chart, setting the charter war in motion.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_charts"]},{"id":"scn_mistral_ledger","title":"The Toll-Master's Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael learns of the Wardens' challenge. Using his ledger-mastery, he finds the weak point in the Wardens' position: their dependence on Cartel-run shipping for cloudstone. He resolves to secure the last stable routes and get Veya's charts.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable skybridge routes before the Wardens' challenge gains support.","conflict":"He admires Veya's skill yet knows her charts could undo the monopoly, and his belief that price equals worth blinds him to the Wardens' appeal to the isles' safety.","outcome":"Kael raises tolls on Warden-bound shipments and orders enforcers to find and bury Veya's charts, escalating the Toll War.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_accusation"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Every Isle Must Choose","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_levy","title":"The Grain Levy Arrives","summary":"Kael's new levy hits The Hollow. Maris, who knows every hidden silo, begins moving grain off the ledgers while Cartel enforcers press the Hollow Circle to side with the charter.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to hide enough grain to keep The Hollow fed through the levy.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are already watching the windmill routes, and Maris trusts so slowly that she hesitates to seek outside help.","outcome":"Maris saves a first stockpile but nearly gets caught, convincing her she needs the unmapped corridors and help she doesn't yet trust.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_ledger"]},{"id":"scn_veya_meets_maris","title":"Trading Winds for Paths","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow seeking safe passage after Cartel enforcers raid her papers at the Academy. She meets Maris and the two trade wind-current knowledge for secret service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a route to carry her charts out of the Cartel's reach, and Maris wants help reading the wind to move grain safely.","conflict":"Maris distrusts outsiders, and Veya, unwilling to admit her chart might be incomplete, withholds a flaw in her readings.","outcome":"They form an uneasy alliance: Maris shows Veya the corridors, and Veya shares wind-sight timings for smuggling runs.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_levy","scn_emberroost_accusation"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_raid","title":"Burned Papers at Silverspine","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Kael arrives in person under charm and legal authority to demand Veya's charts from the Academy. He and Veya clash openly as rivals, and the Academy's scholars are forced to take sides.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to obtain Veya's charts, and Veya wants to keep them out of his hands without surrendering them to the Wardens' politics.","conflict":"Their shared history makes Kael hesitate to use force, while Veya's refusal to concede that one reading is wrong lets Kael exploit the gap.","outcome":"Veya escapes with the core charts but loses her mentor's notes, and the Academy declares for the Wardens, deepening the divide.","depends_on":["scn_veya_meets_maris"]},{"id":"scn_docks_sabotage","title":"Cloudstone on the Docks","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Maris and Veya shadow a Cartel shipment and find cloudstone bound for Emberroost being diverted, proof of sabotage. Kael arrives and the three confront each other in a tense standoff with the docks watching.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want evidence of the Cartel's diversion of forge supplies; Kael wants to stop them leaving with it.","conflict":"Kael must act before witnesses, and Maris's loyalty to home is strained when Veya's plan endangers her smuggling routes.","outcome":"They escape with ledger pages proving the diversion, but Kael tracks Maris's corridors, and the Hollow's routes are exposed.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_raid"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_choice","title":"The Forge Council","summary":"At Emberroost, the Wardens convene an assembly of isle delegates. Veya presents the evidence, and the Wardens want to weaponize it by cutting Cartel crossings. Veya must decide whether to share her full charts with all isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the isles to act on safety using her charts, and Maris wants the Hollow Circle's protection from the levy.","conflict":"The Wardens demand Veya hand over her charts exclusively, tempting her to hoard them as power, while Maris fears losing the Hollow's neutrality.","outcome":"Veya admits one reading was wrong and shares the corrected charts with every isle, forcing each to declare a side and prompting Kael to move on the last stable bridge.","depends_on":["scn_docks_sabotage"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_standoff","title":"Windmills Under Siege","summary":"Kael's enforcers converge on The Hollow, where the last stable bridge route runs through windmill terraces. Maris leads Veya through the hidden corridors while the Hollow Circle stands behind her.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable route; Veya and Maris want to hold it open for all isles.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers outnumber the defenders, and Maris must choose between hiding and standing openly with Veya.","outcome":"Maris stands openly, and the Hollow Circle opens the route, leaving Kael exposed with the charter's authority crumbling.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_choice"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Crossing","summary":"On the failing bridge, Veya uses wind-sight to guide the isles' people across while Kael tries to cut the route. A bridge segment starts to fail, and Kael must choose between control and the lives on the span.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants everyone across safely before the span fails; Kael wants the route sealed under the Cartel.","conflict":"Sealing the route would strand the isles and risk the span, while Veya's old refusal to admit error is tested as one of her readings proves off.","outcome":"Kael lets the route stay open and helps stabilise the cables, giving up his monopoly claim, and the isles cross.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Charter","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mistral_reckoning","title":"A New Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the Cartel's council confronts Kael over losing the monopoly. Kael testifies that control cost more than it gained and proposes tolls shared with the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to salvage a lawful place for the Cartel; Veya wants the charter rewritten to share route knowledge.","conflict":"Cartel princes resent Kael's concession, and Veya must resist the urge to claim the victory as her own.","outcome":"The charter is renegotiated with shared maintenance duties, though Kael loses his toll-master post.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_open_charts","title":"Charts for All","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya opens her charts to every isle, honours her late mentor's theory, and credits Maris and Kael's choice. Maris returns home to The Hollow.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the charts openly and keep the network safe for all.","conflict":"The Academy wants to keep the charts as prestige, and Veya must accept that sharing means losing sole credit.","outcome":"Veya publishes openly, learning that shared truth is safer, and the Academy maintains the charts as a common record.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Quiet Harvest","summary":"At The Hollow, Maris brings the first grain shipment across the reopened route under the revised charter. She accepts that hiding was brave and that standing in the open is too, and she forgives Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed and the levy lifted under the new charter.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and reluctance to forgive make her hesitate to accept Veya's gratitude and the Cartel's new terms.","outcome":"The levy is lifted, the Hollow Circle takes its seat in route governance, and Maris and Veya's friendship is sealed.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_open_charts"]}]}]}
