dger pages proving the diversion, but Kael tracks Maris's corridors, and the Hollow's routes are exposed.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_raid"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_choice","title":"The Forge Council","summary":"At Emberroost, the Wardens convene an assembly of isle delegates. Veya presents the evidence, and the Wardens want to weaponize it by cutting Cartel crossings. Veya must decide whether to share her full charts with all isles.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the isles to act on safety using her charts, and Maris wants the Hollow Circle's protection from the levy.","conflict":"The Wardens demand Veya hand over her charts exclusively, tempting her to hoard them as power, while Maris fears losing the Hollow's neutrality.","outcome":"Veya admits one reading was wrong and shares the corrected charts with every isle, forcing each to declare a side and prompting Kael to move on the last stable bridge.","depends_on":["scn_docks_sabotage"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Stable Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_standoff","title":"Windmills Under Siege","summary":"Kael's enforcers converge on The Hollow, where the last stable bridge route runs through windmill terraces. Maris leads Veya through the hidden corridors while the Hollow Circle stands behind her.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the last stable route; Veya and Maris want to hold it open for all isles.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers outnumber the defenders, and Maris must choose between hiding and standing openly with Veya.","outcome":"Maris stands openly, and the Hollow Circle opens the route, leaving Kael exposed with the charter's authority crumbling.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_choice"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Crossing","summary":"On the failing bridge, Veya uses wind-sight to guide the isles' people across while Kael tries to cut the route. A bridge segment starts to fail, and Kael must choose between control and the lives on the span.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants everyone across safely before the span fails; Kael wants the route sealed under the Cartel.","conflict":"Sealing the route would strand the isles and risk the span, while Veya's old refusal to admit error is tested as one of her readings proves off.","outcome":"Kael lets the route stay open and helps stabilise the cables, giving up his monopoly claim, and the isles cross.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Charter","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mistral_reckoning","title":"A New Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, the Cartel's council confronts Kael over losing the monopoly. Kael testifies that control cost more than it gained and proposes tolls shared with the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to salvage a lawful place for the Cartel; Veya wants the charter rewritten to share route knowledge.","conflict":"Cartel princes resent Kael's concession, and Veya must resist the urge to claim the victory as her own.","outcome":"The charter is renegotiated with shared maintenance duties, though Kael loses his toll-master post.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_open_charts","title":"Charts for All","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya opens her charts to every isle, honours her late mentor's theory, and credits Maris and Kael's choice. Maris returns home to The Hollow.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the charts openly and keep the network safe for all.","conflict":"The Academy wants to keep the charts as prestige, and Veya must accept that sharing means losing sole credit.","outcome":"Veya publishes openly, learning that shared truth is safer, and the Academy maintains the charts as a common record.","depends_on":["scn_mistral_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"The Quiet Harvest","summary":"At The Hollow, Maris brings the first grain shipment across the reopened route under the revised charter. She accepts that hiding was brave and that standing in the open is too, and she forgives Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed and the levy lifted under the new charter.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and reluctance to forgive make her hesitate to accept Veya's gratitude and the Cartel's new terms.","outcome":"The levy is lifted, the Hollow Circle takes its seat in route governance, and Maris and Veya's friendship is sealed.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_open_charts"]}]}]}
