{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Hollow Calm","logline":"When a windless night strands the isles and something ancient stirs in the abandoned skybridge roots, a stubborn cartographer must share her charts with the toll-master who wants them buried, or the breaking bridges will take every isle with them.","theme":"Truths shared are safer than truths hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Wind Stops","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silent_charts","title":"The Silent Charts","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya reads her wind-sight charts as the currents die across the archipelago. The night goes windless, and her instruments show the skybridge roots trembling far below.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Confirm that the calm is the start of the drift her late mentor predicted, and begin charting a safe route through the breaking bridges.","conflict":"Her wind-sight reads nothing in the dead air, and her stubborn certainty clashes with the academy's caution about unverified charts.","outcome":"She finds a pattern of faint pulses rising from the abandoned skybridge roots beneath The Hollow and resolves to investigate."},{"id":"scn_toll_in_the_calm","title":"Toll in the Calm","summary":"At Mistral Docks, becalmed ships crowd the port. Kael raises tolls on the few crossings that still hold, brushing off dockhands' whispers of knocking sounds beneath the bridges.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize control of the last stable skybridge routes before the Cartel's monopoly collapses.","conflict":"Stranded merchants rebel at the tolls, and his belief that price equals worth makes him dismiss the whispers as a bargaining ploy.","outcome":"He learns Veya is mapping the safe routes and decides her charts must belong to the Cartel.","depends_on":["scn_silent_charts"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Roots in the Dark","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_meeting_maris","title":"The Miller's Daughter","summary":"Veya travels the last working bridge to The Hollow, where windmills stand frozen. Maris, hiding grain from Cartel levy agents, agrees to trade her secret service corridors for Veya's current knowledge.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a path to the abandoned roots; Maris wants help keeping The Hollow fed through the crisis.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya is a Cartel spy, while Veya refuses to reveal the full extent of her charts.","outcome":"They form an uneasy alliance, and Maris leads Veya to a corridor descending toward the roots.","depends_on":["scn_silent_charts"]},{"id":"scn_kael_pursues","title":"The Ledger Closes","summary":"Kael crosses to The Hollow with enforcers, using his ledger-mastery to find the weak point in the Hollow Circle's grain arrangements and force a deal.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants Maris to surrender Veya's location and the grain routes.","conflict":"Maris's loyalty to home pulls against her friendship with Veya, and Kael's charm masks a threat she cannot ignore.","outcome":"Maris refuses but is forced to expose one smuggling route, and Kael's enforcers begin tracking the corridor.","depends_on":["scn_toll_in_the_calm","scn_meeting_maris"]},{"id":"scn_into_the_roots","title":"Into the Roots","summary":"Veya and Maris descend the service corridors into the abandoned skybridge roots, finding cloudstone cables knotted and humming with something old and wrong that answers the silence.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Chart the roots and learn what is causing the pulses.","conflict":"Veya's wind-sight is blind without wind, and she refuses to admit her chart is wrong, leading them into a collapsing hollow.","outcome":"They survive by following Maris's pathfinding, and discover the thing is drawn to the still air and to anyone who crosses without repaying their wind-debt.","depends_on":["scn_meeting_maris"]},{"id":"scn_cartel_ambush","title":"The Price of Maps","summary":"Kael's enforcers corner Veya and Maris as they emerge. Kael offers Veya recognition and a Cartel seat in exchange for her charts, playing on her wish for acclaim.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts; Veya wants to escape with them and warn the isles.","conflict":"Veya is tempted by recognition and fears becoming like the cartel leaders, while Kael admires her skill yet cannot let her succeed.","outcome":"Veya refuses and escapes through Maris's corridors, but Kael takes half her charts, and the roots begin to tremble beneath them.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pursues","scn_into_the_roots"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_accuse","title":"Cables of Doubt","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya pleads with the Bridge Wardens to reinforce the bridges, while they accuse Kael of sabotaging their cloudstone supply and distrust her stolen-chart claims.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the Wardens to fortify the weakened bridges; Kael wants to discredit her before them.","conflict":"Veya will not admit that her earlier chart error nearly killed them, so Kael exposes it and the Wardens hesitate under the shadow of the Toll War.","outcome":"The Wardens grant only a few cables and a deadline, and Veya realises that hoarding her knowledge has cost her their trust.","depends_on":["scn_cartel_ambush"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Hollow Calm","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_stirring","title":"The Thing Beneath","summary":"The ancient presence rises through the roots under The Hollow, severing cables and tearing at the bridges as the air stays dead. Kael's Cartel convoy is trapped on a failing crossing.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to guide everyone off the failing bridges; Kael wants to hold the last stable route for the Cartel.","conflict":"Kael refuses to surrender the route, and Veya's pride keeps her from asking him to share the charts he took.","outcome":"The convoy is nearly lost, forcing Veya and Kael into a desperate truce.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_accuse"]},{"id":"scn_shared_charts","title":"The Shared Chart","summary":"Veya gives her full charts to Kael and the Wardens, and Kael surrenders control of the routes. Maris guides them through the unmapped corridors while Veya reads the faint wind-colours to lead the isles clear.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Combine the charts, routes, and corridors to evacuate the failing bridges.","conflict":"Admitting error and surrendering control goes against Veya's flaw and Kael's belief that price equals worth, and the roots lash at every step.","outcome":"A breath of wind returns as the crossings clear, driving the presence back into the roots, though the bridges are badly damaged.","depends_on":["scn_the_stirring"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Wind Left","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_cost_of_control","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel's ruin and the Wardens' demands. He opens the routes and forgives the debts of the stranded.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to salvage the Cartel's standing without his monopoly.","conflict":"The Cartel princes resent his concession, and Veya's charts now belong to everyone.","outcome":"Kael accepts that control cost more than it gained, and the Toll War ends in a shared-route agreement.","depends_on":["scn_shared_charts"]},{"id":"scn_new_currents","title":"New Currents","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya publishes her charts openly and honours her mentor's theory. Maris returns to The Hollow, where the windmills turn again, and the grain levy is eased.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the charts for all; Maris wants her isle fed and safe.","conflict":"Veya must admit her mistakes publicly, and Maris must decide whether to trust her friendship with Veya beyond the crisis.","outcome":"Veya learns that shared truths are safer, Maris sees that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and the isles drift on under a wary wind.","depends_on":["scn_cost_of_control"]}]}]}

