ing together they stabilise the bridge, and Kael realises control cost him more than it gained.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Stabilise the failing span before it severs.","conflict":"Each must rely on a person they distrust, and Kael's price-equals-worth habit tempts him to bargain at the worst moment.","outcome":"The bridge holds, and Kael relinquishes his claim on the route.","depends_on":["scn_climax_crossing"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"Shared Routes","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_res_silverspine_share","title":"Charts for All","summary":"Veya presents the corrected charts at Silverspine Academy and shares them openly with the Wardens and the Hollow Circle. She credits Maris and acknowledges her mentor's theory was only partly right.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Share the charts openly so all isles can use safe routes.","conflict":"Some scholars resist because the charts contradict their records, and Veya must admit her earlier error publicly.","outcome":"The charts are adopted network-wide and the Wardens begin reinforcing routes.","depends_on":["scn_climax_cooperation"]},{"id":"scn_res_docks_toll","title":"A Fairer Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael faces the Cartel and cuts the skybridge toll and lifts the grain levy in exchange for labour on bridge repairs under the wind-debt rule. Cartel princes grumble but are bound by the stability he proved.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"End the toll war on terms that keep the bridges standing.","conflict":"Cartel princes resist losing profit and Kael's old habit of valuing everything by price resurfaces.","outcome":"The toll is lowered and the levy lifted, easing the Toll War and the Grain Levy.","depends_on":["scn_climax_cooperation"]},{"id":"scn_res_hollow_harvest","title":"Windmills Turning","summary":"In The Hollow, grain flows free