slowly and suspects Veya of being a Cartel spy, while Veya's reluctance to share her whole chart strains the bargain.","outcome":"They strike an alliance: Veya refines the chart using Maris's corridors, and Maris's smuggling grows more efficient.","depends_on":["scn_forge_accusation","scn_hollow_levy"]},{"id":"scn_enforcer_raid","title":"The Raid on the Granaries","summary":"Kael, who has learned of the smuggling from the Cartel's ledgers, sends enforcers to the docks to intercept a grain shipment and, in doing so, discovers that Maris's routes line up with Veya's chart.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to stop the smuggling and trace its source. Maris wants her grain to reach The Hollow.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery finds the weak point in her arrangement, and Maris has to choose between abandoning the shipment and exposing Veya.","outcome":"Maris escapes with part of the grain, but Kael confirms that Veya is behind the new routes and Maris learns the Cartel is closing in.","depends_on":["scn_secret_paths"]},{"id":"scn_mentor_notes","title":"The Mentor's Last Notes","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya finds her mentor's notes and realises one of her own assumptions was wrong, which would put the chart's safest route in danger.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to finalise the route, and Maris wants to know whether it is safe for the Hollow's grain.","conflict":"Veya cannot admit her error until Maris's practical knowledge of the corridors exposes it, and Maris's trust in her is shaken.","outcome":"Veya corrects the chart, and the two agree that the Cartel must be confronted before the route is used, but Maris is still wary of Veya.","depends_on":["scn_enforcer_raid"]},{"id":"scn_kael_offer","title":"An Offer at the Docks","summary":"Kael confronts Veya at Mistral Docks and offers her recognition, funding and a place in the Cartel in exchange for the charts, arguing that the tolls are what keep the bridges repaired.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants the charts and Veya's cooperation, and Veya wants to leave with her work and her freedom.","conflict":"Veya is tempted by the recognition she craves, and Kael admires her skill but cannot let her succeed on her own terms.","outcome":"Veya refuses, but Kael reveals the toll revenue really does fund the Wardens' repairs, which leaves her rattled.","depends_on":["scn_mentor_notes"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_public_chart","title":"Charts in the Open","summary":"Veya chooses to share her complete chart with the Bridge Wardens and the isles at Emberroost, revealing which routes will fail and which will hold, and the Wardens confront Kael over the tolls.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to make the chart public so that no one controls it. Kael wants to stop her and keep the Cartel's hold on the routes.","conflict":"Kael argues that the tolls repair the bridges while Maris shows that the levy is starving The Hollow, and Veya must weigh both truths.","outcome":"The chart is shared and Kael's monopoly collapses, while the Wardens and the Hollow Circle force him to answer for what the tolls cost.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offer","scn_mentor_notes"]},{"id":"scn_kael_choice","title":"The Tollmaster's Bargain","summary":"With a failing bridge between Emberroost and the Hollow, Kael sees that his control cannot save it. He is asked to choose between the Cartel's gain and the isles, and he opens the stable routes and forgoes the toll to repair the bridge.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to keep the last stable route under Cartel control, and Veya wants it repaired and open to everyone.","conflict":"His belief that price equals worth fights with his admiration for Veya, and the wind-debt rule means every crossing still has to be repaid.","outcome":"Kael waives the tolls for the repair crossing and the bridge holds, at the cost of his monopoly, and the isles are left unsure whether to condemn him.","depends_on":["scn_public_chart"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Isles Owe","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_relief","title":"Grain Across the Bridge","summary":"Grain flows openly from The Hollow across the repaired bridge, and Maris sees the levy lifted and her smuggling no longer needed, while the isles argue over whether Kael is villain or saviour.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to feed The Hollow openly and decide whether she can forgive Veya.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and rarely forgives, and the Hollow Circle resents that the relief came from Kael.","outcome":"Maris accepts that hiding was brave but standing in the open is possible, and she renews her friendship with Veya.","depends_on":["scn_kael_choice"]},{"id":"scn_new_ledger","title":"A New Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael meets the Cartel and the Wardens to set shared terms for toll and repair under the wind-debt rule, accepting that control costs more than it gains.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to salvage a place for the Cartel in the new order.","conflict":"The Cartel's merchant princes resent the loss of the monopoly, and the Wardens and Hollow Circle distrust any terms he offers.","outcome":"A shared compact is agreed, with tolls tied to repair and the levy ended, and Kael is left diminished but useful.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_relief"]},{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"Mapping the Drift","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine to teach the new charts and admits publicly that she was wrong about her first route, and she looks ahead to a drifting archipelago that will have to be kept together.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share her charts openly and credit those who helped her.","conflict":"Her pride resists acknowledging her mistakes, and the isles remain divided about whether Kael deserves forgiveness.","outcome":"Veya credits Maris and her mentor, the charts are kept open, and the isles accept a bittersweet peace in which the bridges hold but the drift continues.","depends_on":["scn_new_ledger"]}]}]}
</Output>
