{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Phantom Heir","logline":"As the skybridges of Aetheria begin to fail, cartographer Veya races to chart a safe route while Cartel toll-master Kael tries to seize the last stable crossings, and both must decide whether truth is shared or controlled before the archipelago is cut apart.","theme":"Truths shared save more than truths hoarded","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Fraying Threads","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_survey","title":"The Drifting Chart","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya finishes a new chart using her wind-sight. It shows the skybridges failing faster than anyone has admitted, and it supports her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Complete a chart of the failing skybridge network that proves her mentor's drift theory.","conflict":"Her wind-sight readings contradict the Academy's official charts, and her stubborn pride makes her refuse to consider that she might have misread a current.","outcome":"Veya finishes a chart showing the main bridges failing within a season, and decides to take it to the docks to find a safe route."},{"id":"scn_docks_toll","title":"The Price of Crossing","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael charms and squeezes merchants while raising skybridge tolls. He hears rumours of a Silverspine chart that threatens the Cartel's plans and sets out to find its maker.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Lock down the last stable skybridge routes under Cartel control by raising tolls.","conflict":"Merchants and Bridge Wardens protest that the tolls add to wind-debt they cannot repay within a season, and Kael's habit of equating price with worth blinds him to their desperation.","outcome":"Kael learns of Veya's chart and resolves to buy or bury it, which sets up the Toll War's next stage."},{"id":"scn_docks_meeting","title":"Old Apprentices","summary":"Veya reaches Mistral Docks to look for a trade route and meets Kael, her former fellow apprentice. He offers to buy her charts and promises to fund her work. She refuses, and the offer shows her how much he already knows.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to secure passage for her survey. Kael wants to acquire her charts.","conflict":"Kael's offer is tempting, and Veya fears becoming ambitious like the Cartel leaders. She will not let him control her work.","outcome":"Veya refuses and leaves with her chart. Kael quietly marks her as a threat and orders Cartel enforcers to watch her.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_survey","scn_docks_toll"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Breaking Bridges","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_refuge","title":"Grain and Secrets","summary":"Pursued by enforcers, Veya flees to The Hollow. There Maris, the miller's daughter, hides her among the windmills. Veya trades wind-current knowledge for Maris's knowledge of the unmapped service corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a hiding place and a way to continue charting. Maris wants to protect The Hollow from the Cartel's grain levy.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya will bring the Cartel down on her isle. Veya's stubbornness makes her reluctant to accept help.","outcome":"They form an alliance. Maris agrees to guide Veya along her hidden corridors in exchange for Veya's wind-current readings to protect smuggling runs.","depends_on":["scn_docks_meeting"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_sabotage","title":"Cables Cut at Emberroost","summary":"Veya and Maris travel to Emberroost and find that forge supplies for the skybridge cables have been tampered with. The Wardens suspect Kael. Veya sees her chart is already coming true as a bridge starts to unravel.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Confirm which bridges are failing and warn the Bridge Wardens.","conflict":"The Wardens blame the Cartel and want to act rashly, and open flame is forbidden outside shielded forge-pits, which limits any hasty repair. Maris fears exposing her smuggling routes.","outcome":"They gather proof that supplies are being diverted and that the chart is accurate. Veya realises she needs to confront Kael's role directly.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_refuge"]},{"id":"scn_levy_squeeze","title":"The Levy Tightens","summary":"Kael uses his ledger-mastery to find the weak points in The Hollow's trade arrangements and enforces the grain levy. Enforcers close in on Maris's smuggling routes.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to force The Hollow into compliance and flush out Veya. Maris wants to keep grain moving.","conflict":"Kael's charm clashes with Maris's loyalty and her reluctance to forgive. His enforcers threaten the windmill families.","outcome":"Maris is forced to expose a silo to save her people, which strains her trust in everyone. Kael learns Veya is heading to Silverspine.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_sabotage"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_archive","title":"The Mentor's Archive","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and finds her mentor's notes. They show the chart is correct but only one route can hold, and only if the Wardens and traders cooperate. Her refusal to admit an early error in her own reading nearly costs her the route.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Find the safe route through the failing network using the mentor's notes.","conflict":"Veya will not admit that an early reading was wrong, and the corrected route is far less direct. Maris is torn between helping her and going back to The Hollow.","outcome":"Veya admits the error, with Maris's help, and finds a single viable route. It runs through the same crossings Kael is trying to seize.","depends_on":["scn_levy_squeeze"]},{"id":"scn_rival_confrontation","title":"Ledger and Chart","summary":"Kael confronts Veya at Silverspine and offers a bargain: give the Cartel exclusive control of the route, and he will shield The Hollow from the levy. He admires her skill but cannot let her succeed on her own terms.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the route exclusively for the Cartel. Veya wants it open to all.","conflict":"His offer would save Maris's home at the cost of Veya's principles, and Maris must choose between her loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya.","outcome":"Veya refuses to bury the route, and Maris, who stays loyal to both, backs her. Kael leaves vowing to take the bridges by force. All three now race for the same crossing.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_archive"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_gathering","title":"Rallying the Isles","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Veya publicly shares her chart with merchants, Wardens and Hollow Circle members, while Maris uses her corridors to bring grain and allies through. Kael's hold on information starts to slip.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the route widely so it cannot be buried. Kael wants to stop the broadcast and seize the route.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers and his ledger-mastery turn merchants' wind-debts against the plan. Veya's pride must give way to relying on others.","outcome":"The merchants split, and enough of them back Veya that the Cartel cannot close the route at the docks. Kael falls back to the last crossing to take it by force.","depends_on":["scn_rival_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_crossing","title":"The Last Skybridge","summary":"At Emberroost, the last stable skybridge begins to fail as Kael's party and Veya's convoy meet on it. Veya reads the wind currents to hold the bridge while Maris guides people through the service corridors. Kael sees that seizing the bridge would collapse it.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get the convoy across and save the route. Kael tries to seize the crossing.","conflict":"Holding the bridge needs Kael's cooperation, but he equates control with worth. Open flame is forbidden, so he cannot cut the cables as he intended. Wind-debt stacks up as the crossings continue.","outcome":"Kael stops, recognises that control costs more than it gains, and lets the convoy cross. The route holds and the Cartel's monopoly breaks.","depends_on":["scn_docks_gathering"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wardens_accord","title":"The Wardens' Accord","summary":"At Emberroost the Wardens, the Hollow Circle and a chastened Kael negotiate how the route and its wind-debts will be shared. Kael gives up his monopoly in return for a fair toll.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle who maintains the route and how tolls and wind-debts are shared.","conflict":"The Wardens distrust Kael after the sabotage, and Maris is slow to forgive. Kael's habit of pricing everything makes the talks fraught.","outcome":"A shared accord is signed. Tolls are capped, the grain levy is eased, and Kael takes on debt of his own for the sabotage.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_atlas","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya publishes the chart openly, crediting her mentor. She accepts that some truths are safer shared and gets recognition without the ambition she feared.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Publish the chart and honour her mentor's theory.","conflict":"The Academy wants to hold the chart back, and Kael's rivalry lingers, as he still half-wishes he had controlled it.","outcome":"The chart is released to all isles, and Kael, now a rival who respects her, helps distribute it.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_accord"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Hiding and Standing","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris watches the first free grain barges leave and shares her secret corridors with the Circle. She understands that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and Veya visits as a friend.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Make sure The Hollow is fed and end her life as a smuggler.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to trust outsiders, and her secret corridors must now be shared.","outcome":"Maris opens her routes to the Circle and forgives Veya. The Hollow is secure and the isles remain bound together.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_atlas"]}]}]}
