"]},{"id":"scn_rival_confrontation","title":"Ledger and Chart","summary":"Kael confronts Veya at Silverspine and offers a bargain: give the Cartel exclusive control of the route, and he will shield The Hollow from the levy. He admires her skill but cannot let her succeed on her own terms.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants the route exclusively for the Cartel. Veya wants it open to all.","conflict":"His offer would save Maris's home at the cost of Veya's principles, and Maris must choose between her loyalty to home and her friendship with Veya.","outcome":"Veya refuses to bury the route, and Maris, who stays loyal to both, backs her. Kael leaves vowing to take the bridges by force. All three now race for the same crossing.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_archive"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Crossing","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_gathering","title":"Rallying the Isles","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Veya publicly shares her chart with merchants, Wardens and Hollow Circle members, while Maris uses her corridors to bring grain and allies through. Kael's hold on information starts to slip.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the route widely so it cannot be buried. Kael wants to stop the broadcast and seize the route.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers and his ledger-mastery turn merchants' wind-debts against the plan. Veya's pride must give way to relying on others.","outcome":"The merchants split, and enough of them back Veya that the Cartel cannot close the route at the docks. Kael falls back to the last crossing to take it by force.","depends_on":["scn_rival_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_crossing","title":"The Last Skybridge","summary":"At Emberroost, the last stable skybridge begins to fail as Kael's party and Veya's convoy meet on it. Veya reads the wind currents to hold the bridge while Maris guides people through the service corridors. Kael sees that seizing the bridge would collapse it.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get the convoy across and save the route. Kael tries to seize the crossing.","conflict":"Holding the bridge needs Kael's cooperation, but he equates control with worth. Open flame is forbidden, so he cannot cut the cables as he intended. Wind-debt stacks up as the crossings continue.","outcome":"Kael stops, recognises that control costs more than it gains, and lets the convoy cross. The route holds and the Cartel's monopoly breaks.","depends_on":["scn_docks_gathering"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"New Currents","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_wardens_accord","title":"The Wardens' Accord","summary":"At Emberroost the Wardens, the Hollow Circle and a chastened Kael negotiate how the route and its wind-debts will be shared. Kael gives up his monopoly in return for a fair toll.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Settle who maintains the route and how tolls and wind-debts are shared.","conflict":"The Wardens distrust Kael after the sabotage, and Maris is slow to forgive. Kael's habit of pricing everything makes the talks fraught.","outcome":"A shared accord is signed. Tolls are capped, the grain levy is eased, and Kael takes on debt of his own for the sabotage.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_atlas","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya publishes the chart openly, crediting her mentor. She accepts that some truths are safer shared and gets recognition without the ambition she feared.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Publish the chart and honour her mentor's theory.","conflict":"The Academy wants to hold the chart back, and Kael's rivalry lingers, as he still half-wishes he had controlled it.","outcome":"The chart is released to all isles, and Kael, now a rival who respects her, helps distribute it.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_accord"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Hiding and Standing","summary":"In The Hollow, Maris watches the first free grain barges leave and shares her secret corridors with the Circle. She understands that hiding can be as brave as standing still, and Veya visits as a friend.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Make sure The Hollow is fed and end her life as a smuggler.","conflict":"Maris still struggles to trust outsiders, and her secret corridors must now be shared.","outcome":"Maris opens her routes to the Circle and forgives Veya. The Hollow is secure and the isles remain bound together.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_atlas"]}]}]}
